# 🔴 Red Team Lab – Metasploitable2

## 📌 Overview  
Performed a practical **red team security assessment** using Kali Linux against Metasploitable2 in a controlled lab.  
Covers full attack workflow from **reconnaissance to post-exploitation and reporting**.

---

## 🎯 Objectives  
- Identify vulnerable services  
- Exploit real-world vulnerabilities  
- Gain and analyze shell access  
- Perform post-exploitation  
- Test password security  
- Simulate malware detection  
- Map to MITRE ATT&CK  

---

## ⚙️ Lab Setup  
- **Attacker:** Kali Linux  
- **Target:** Metasploitable2  
- **Environment:** Virtual Lab  

---

## 🚀 Tasks Performed  
- 🔍 Reconnaissance (port & service scanning)  
- 🛠️ Vulnerability Assessment  
- 💥 Exploitation (FTP, Samba)  
- 🧠 Post-Exploitation (permissions, SUID)  
- 🔁 Reverse Shell  
- 🔐 Password Testing (default credentials)  
- 🦠 Malware Simulation  
- 🧩 MITRE ATT&CK Mapping  

---

## 📊 Key Findings  
- Outdated services are easily exploitable  
- Default credentials allow direct access  
- Multiple attack paths exist  
- Weak system hardening increases risk  

---

## 🛡️ Recommendations  
- Update or remove vulnerable services  
- Disable insecure protocols (e.g., Telnet)  
- Enforce strong password policies  
- Perform regular vulnerability scans  
- Monitor network and authentication activity  

---

